CM_ "ARS510 low-level frame-local DBC. This file intentionally exposes only raw transport bytes for 0x80/0x85, observed 0x81/0x86 record-cycle markers, pair-local track identity/age fields for 0x191/0x193, startup and sync/debug structure, and recurring raw candidate frames. Multi-frame reconstruction, object geometry, publication, selection, global lifecycle, and quality/state semantics remain parser-runtime owned. See docs/ in the ars510-radar repo.";
CM_ BO_ 128 "ARS510 ID80 segmented object-record frame. Runtime reassembly starts on bytes 0x12 0xE4 and appends bytes 1..7 from 106 frames into a 742-byte record.";
CM_ BO_ 133 "ARS510 ID85 segmented metadata-record frame. Runtime reassembly starts on bytes 0x10 0x90 and appends bytes 1..7 from 21 frames into a 147-byte record.";
CM_ BO_ 129 "ARS510 ID80 record-cycle companion marker. Across the recorded drives, one fixed 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 frame follows each ID80 12 E4 record start within 20 ms. Framing/synchronization only; not object validity, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or geometry.";
CM_ BO_ 134 "ARS510 ID85 record-cycle companion marker. Across the recorded drives, one fixed 30 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 frame follows each ID85 10 90 record start within 20 ms. Framing/synchronization only; not object validity, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or geometry.";
CM_ BO_ 256 "ARS510 0x100 startup/context frame. The first big-endian 16-bit word is normally zero; one recorded startup frame contains 0xFFFF. Bytes 2..6 are zero on every recorded frame. Startup/configuration structure only; no object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 257 "ARS510 0x101 startup-state frame. State 0x1D changes once to 0x11 exactly 70 ms before A197_STARTUP_PHASE1 on the recorded drives. State 0x21 is a rare unresolved transient. Bytes 1..5 are reserved zero; no object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 258 "ARS510 0x102 sparse state/context frame. Only bits 11, 14, and 21 change on recorded drives; their Toyota cruise/brake comparisons do not support semantic naming. All other bits are reserved zero. Context metadata only; no object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 259 "ARS510 0x103 reserved guard frame. Both payload bytes are zero on every recorded drive frame; no object or operational semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 384 "ARS510 0x180 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 400 "ARS510 0x190 radar-cycle timing header. Bytes 2..5 are a observed big-endian microsecond timestamp and byte 6 high nibble is a modulo-16 rolling counter advancing +3 per nominal cycle; synchronization metadata only, not object semantics.";
CM_ BO_ 401 "ARS510 0x191 pair-track summary frame. Sentinel payload FEFEFEFCFCFFFEFF. Byte 0 bits 1..7 are a score-like 91..100 active code, byte 1 bits 1..7 are a saturating pair-local track-age counter, and byte 3 bits 2..7 are a pair-local track identity code. Bytes 4, 6, and 7 form an identity-stable descriptor tuple with unresolved OEM meaning; byte 5 is a separate dynamic code. These fields are not promoted as confidence, validity, publication, selection, dimensions, or class truth.";
CM_ BO_ 402 "ARS510 0x192 target summary (4 bytes). Sentinel 00FF00FF = no target. A filtered summary of the target the radar selects itself (probably for ACC / pre-collision), NOT a better lead measurement: bytes 0-1 are a big-endian distance of about 3/64 m per code, heavily smoothed and lagging the 0x80 track by 10-15 m in closings; byte 2 is a lateral bin of that target (7/8 own lane, 6 and 9 adjacent lanes, 10-13 far left, 2-5 oncoming side); byte 3 unknown. It matches some 0x80 track within 1.5 m only 18-39% of the time. 0x191 is its companion (score, age, id).";
CM_ BO_ 403 "ARS510 0x193 pair-track summary frame. Sentinel payload FEFEFEFCFCFFFEFF. Byte 0 bits 1..7 are a score-like 91..100 active code, byte 1 bits 1..7 are a saturating pair-local track-age counter, and byte 3 bits 2..7 are a pair-local track identity code. Bytes 4, 6, and 7 form an identity-stable descriptor tuple with unresolved OEM meaning; byte 5 is a separate dynamic code. These fields are not promoted as confidence, validity, publication, selection, dimensions, or class truth.";
CM_ BO_ 404 "ARS510 0x194 target summary, same shape as 0x192 (second selected target?). Not characterised; 0x193 is its companion.";
CM_ BO_ 405 "ARS510 0x195 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 406 "ARS510 0x196 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 407 "ARS510 0x197 startup-phase frame. Bit 8 is zero only during the initial recorded-drive startup interval and then changes once to one without reverting; startup metadata only, not object validity, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or geometry.";
CM_ BO_ 408 "ARS510 0x198 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 514 "ARS510 0x202 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Byte 1 high nibble is a observed modulo-16 counter candidate; no object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 528 "ARS510 0x210 replicated Toyota road-sign-assist context frame. Byte-0 bit 0 mirrors speed-sign presence, byte 1 mirrors RSA1.SPDVAL1, and byte-5 bit 6 mirrors RSA3.TSRMSW on the recorded drives. The speed unit is selected externally by RSA2.SPDUNT. Not radar object semantics.";
CM_ BO_ 565 "ARS510 0x235 companion/debug frame. Byte 1 is split into a recorded low-nibble mux and high-nibble rolling counter; no object geometry, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or candidate-generation truth is promoted here.";
CM_ BO_ 567 "ARS510 0x237 companion/debug frame. Byte 1 is split into a recorded low-nibble mux and high-nibble rolling counter; no object geometry, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or candidate-generation truth is promoted here.";
CM_ BO_ 569 "ARS510 0x239 companion/debug frame. Byte 1 is split into a recorded low-nibble mux and high-nibble rolling counter; no object geometry, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or candidate-generation truth is promoted here.";
CM_ BO_ 571 "ARS510 0x23B companion/debug frame. Three-byte member of the synchronized 0x23x family; byte 1 is split into mux/counter nibbles, with no direct geometry, lifecycle, publication, selection, quality, or candidate-generation truth promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 573 "ARS510 0x23D companion/debug frame. Route evidence recorded it as an all-zero guard/debug frame; no object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 576 "ARS510 0x240 synchronized mirror frame. Byte 0 carries a observed 3-bit mux phase; bytes 1..6 are two exactly equal raw BE24 words and byte 7 is reserved zero. The four mirror addresses are byte-identical whenever observed together; no geometry, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 577 "ARS510 0x241 synchronized mirror frame. Byte 0 carries a observed 3-bit mux phase; bytes 1..6 are two exactly equal raw BE24 words and byte 7 is reserved zero. The four mirror addresses are byte-identical whenever observed together; no geometry, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 580 "ARS510 0x244 synchronized mirror frame. Byte 0 carries a observed 3-bit mux phase; bytes 1..6 are two exactly equal raw BE24 words and byte 7 is reserved zero. The four mirror addresses are byte-identical whenever observed together; no geometry, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 581 "ARS510 0x245 synchronized mirror frame. Byte 0 carries a observed 3-bit mux phase; bytes 1..6 are two exactly equal raw BE24 words and byte 7 is reserved zero. The four mirror addresses are byte-identical whenever observed together; no geometry, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 584 "ARS510 0x248 synchronized startup/event context frame. Byte 0 carries startup/status context and the common 3-bit mux phase; byte-2 bit 0 is a one-way startup phase 2, and byte-6 bit 1 is a rare isolated event pulse of unresolved meaning. No object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 589 "ARS510 0x24D recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 591 "ARS510 0x24F recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 1280 "ARS510 0x500 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw-byte coverage only; no radar object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 1281 "ARS510 0x501 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw coverage plus reviewed status/mux context metadata; no geometry, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 1282 "ARS510 0x502 slow-state bus-1 frame. Observed on the recorded drives and on five independent native segments at a 3.000 s median interarrival with DLC 8. Byte 0 is 0x19 and bytes 4..7 are <unit-specific 32-bit constant, redacted> on every nonzero frame of all three drives; both constants are documented, not enforced. Bytes 2..3 are a carry-verified big-endian pair, while bytes 0..1 have no observed carry excitation and are therefore not grouped into a 16-bit field. The two varying fields drift by small signed steps with plateaus up to about 12 minutes and no route-stable relationship to each other. Source ECU, units, scale, and signedness are unresolved; no geometry, velocity, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ BO_ 1664 "ARS510 0x680 recurring bus-1 candidate frame. Observed raw coverage plus reviewed status/mux context metadata; no geometry, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, selection, or candidate-generation semantics are promoted.";
CM_ SG_ 514 A202_CHECK_BYTE8 "0x202 byte 0. Determined entirely by A202_COUNTER4 on the recorded drives via the fixed map 0:0x10 1:0x8D 2:0x37 3:0xAA 4:0x5E 5:0xC3 6:0x79 7:0xE4 8:0x8C 9:0x11 10:0xAB 11:0x36 12:0xC2 13:0x5F 14:0xE5 15:0x78, and byte 0 of a counter and of its XOR-9 partner differ only in bit 0, which is a check-byte signature. Frame-check candidate only: the payload it covers is constant on the recorded drives, so neither the algorithm nor its behavior over a varying payload is identified. Do not use it to reject frames.";
CM_ SG_ 514 A202_B1_RESERVED_ZERO4 "0x202 byte-1 low nibble. Zero on every recorded bus-1 frame; reserved packed-boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 514 A202_B2_B4_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE24 "0x202 bytes 2..4, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant 0x036D80 on every recorded bus-1 frame of the recorded drives. Documented, not enforced.";
CM_ SG_ 591 A24F_B0_RESERVED_ZERO6 "0x24F byte-0 bits 0..5. Zero on every recorded bus-1 frame; reserved packed-boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 591 A24F_STARTUP_PHASE1 "0x24F byte-0 bit 6. Zero for the first 24 frames of the short recorded drive (0.221 s to 0.911 s) and then one without reverting; one on every long-route frame, which begins after power-on. Startup/debug context only, matching A197_STARTUP_PHASE1; not radar-ready, object validity, lifecycle, publication, selection, or quality truth.";
CM_ SG_ 591 A24F_B0_RESERVED_ZERO1 "0x24F byte-0 bit 7. Zero on every recorded bus-1 frame; reserved packed-boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 1281 A501_B0_B3_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE32 "0x501 bytes 0..3, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant 0xFFF0FFF0 on every recorded bus-1 frame of the recorded drives. An all-ones-style word like this is often a not-available encoding, but that is not established here; documented, not enforced.";
CM_ SG_ 1281 A501_B4_OBSERVED_CONSTANT8 "0x501 byte 4. Observed constant 0x70 on every recorded bus-1 frame of the recorded drives. Documented, not enforced.";
CM_ SG_ 1281 A501_B6_OBSERVED_CONSTANT8 "0x501 byte 6. Observed constant 0x00 on every recorded bus-1 frame of the recorded drives. Documented, not enforced.";
CM_ SG_ 384 A180_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE40 "0x180 full payload, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant 0xCFC0000000 on all 214,731 recorded bus-1 frames of the recorded drives, so this frame carries no varying field on the recorded evidence and generic raw bytes would overstate its content. The constant is documented, not enforced: any value still decodes, and a route that varies this frame falsifies the observation. The first frame on a recorded drive instead carries 0xFFC0000000, an initialization-like payload. That is an observation, not a drop rule: it is preserved and decoded like any other payload.";
CM_ SG_ 408 A198_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE8 "0x198 full payload, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant 0x10 on all 214,744 recorded bus-1 frames of the recorded drives, so this frame carries no varying field on the recorded evidence and generic raw bytes would overstate its content. The constant is documented, not enforced: any value still decodes, and a route that varies this frame falsifies the observation. The first frame on a recorded drive instead carries 0x00, an initialization-like payload. That is an observation, not a drop rule: it is preserved and decoded like any other payload.";
CM_ SG_ 573 A23D_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE64 "0x23D full payload, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant 0x0000000000000000 on all 644,232 recorded bus-1 frames of the recorded drives, so this frame carries no varying field on the recorded evidence and generic raw bytes would overstate its content. The constant is documented, not enforced: any value still decodes, and a route that varies this frame falsifies the observation.";
CM_ SG_ 589 A24D_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE56 "0x24D full payload, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant 0x00000000000056 on all 12,885 recorded bus-1 frames of the recorded drives, so this frame carries no varying field on the recorded evidence and generic raw bytes would overstate its content. The constant is documented, not enforced: any value still decodes, and a route that varies this frame falsifies the observation.";
CM_ SG_ 1280 A500_OBSERVED_CONSTANT_BE48 "0x500 full payload, unsigned big-endian. Observed constant <unit-specific 48-bit constant, redacted> on all 25,768 recorded bus-1 frames of the recorded drives, so this frame carries no varying field on the recorded evidence and generic raw bytes would overstate its content. The constant is documented, not enforced: any value still decodes, and a route that varies this frame falsifies the observation. The first frame on a recorded drive instead carries 0xFFF8FFC0FFC0, an initialization-like payload. That is an observation, not a drop rule: it is preserved and decoded like any other payload.";
CM_ SG_ 405 A195_WORD0_CODE16 "0x195 bits 0..15 MSB-first, unsigned big-endian. Idle payload value 32766. Unresolved numeric code. Boundary comes from bits that stay constant across all 61 active frames of the recorded drives and also hold when idle frames are included. Dead end D-036 (docs/08_dead_ends.md) retired the object-summary and direct-geometry readings of this pair and this field does not reopen them: not range, azimuth, lateral, velocity, validity, quality, lifecycle, publication, or selection.";
CM_ SG_ 405 A195_B2_RESERVED_ZERO3 "0x195 bits 16..18 MSB-first, unsigned big-endian. Idle payload value 0. Held at zero on every non-idle frame of the recorded drives with the power-on frame excluded; reserved packed-boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 405 A195_B2_RESERVED_ONE2 "0x195 bits 19..20 MSB-first, unsigned big-endian. Idle payload value 3. Held at one on every non-idle frame of the recorded drives with the power-on frame excluded; reserved packed-boundary guard.";
