CM_ SG_ 1282 A502_B0_CONST8 "0x502 byte 0. Observed 0x19 on every nonzero frame of the recorded drives and five independent native segments. Exposed separately because bytes 0..1 show no carry excitation, so a 16-bit boundary is unproven; the constant is not enforced and the all-zero startup payload is preserved.";
CM_ SG_ 1282 A502_SLOW_CODE0_B1 "0x502 byte 1. Slowly varying raw code; observed 0x69..0x92 across three drives with mostly plus or minus one steps and long plateaus. Units, scale, signedness, and semantics unresolved; context/debug only.";
CM_ SG_ 1282 A502_SLOW_CODE1_BE16 "0x502 bytes 2..3, unsigned big-endian. The byte boundary is carry-verified: 80 byte-3 to byte-2 carry/borrow events on the long recorded drive. Observed 4308..4408 across three drives with small signed steps; it changes more often than byte 1 and the two fields have no route-stable relationship. Units, scale, signedness, and semantics unresolved; context/debug only.";
CM_ SG_ 1282 A502_TAIL_CONST_BE32 "0x502 bytes 4..7, unsigned big-endian. Observed <unit-specific 32-bit constant, redacted> on every nonzero frame of the recorded drives and five independent native segments. Retained as a raw field so the constant is documented rather than enforced; no object semantics are promoted.";
CM_ SG_ 528 A210_RSA_SPEED_SIGN_PRESENT1 "0x210 byte-0 bit 0. Across drives, replica of whether Toyota RSA1.TSGN1 carries recorded speed-sign type 36; road-sign context only, not radar object validity or publication.";
