CM_ SG_ 401 A191_B0_RESERVED0 "0x191 byte 0 low bit. Zero on all recorded active and sentinel frames; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_SCORE_CODE7 "0x191 bits 1|7. Exact score-like code: active values are 91..100, same-identity transitions are almost always stable or unit steps, and sentinel value is 127. Route-stable survival stratification exists, but route-heldout evidence does not justify naming this OEM confidence or using it as validity, publication, or selection truth.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_B1_RESERVED0 "0x191 byte 1 low bit. Zero on all recorded active and sentinel frames; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_TRACK_AGE7 "0x191 bits 9|7. Track-age-like counter: usually advances across nominal 60 ms cycles while identity is stable, plateaus at 126, and is 127 in the sentinel. Repeats and jumps occur; age may advance while the co-envelope 0x190 timestamp repeats. Native same-tag unsaturated examples advance through intervening sentinel output cycles; sentinel return need not reset age. Not elapsed time, a freshness gate, physical identity proof, or full OEM lifecycle/publication truth. Identity can migrate between output pairs.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_B3_RESERVED0_2 "0x191 byte 3 low two bits. Zero on all recorded active and sentinel frames; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_TRACK_ID6 "0x191 bits 26|6. Track identity code exposed at this output pair; recorded reciprocal and additional-route nonreciprocal migrations support following a code across pairs. Pair changes do not prove track birth or death. Duplicate codes, reuse, physical association and ID80 correspondence remain unresolved; not a globally stable openpilot track identifier or solved selection rule.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_B4_RESERVED0_2 "0x191 byte 4 low two bits. Zero on every recorded active paired row; packed-field boundary guard. Sentinel value is zero.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_DESCRIPTOR0_CODE6 "0x191 bits 34|6. First member of an identity-stable three-code descriptor tuple. Active values are 18, 22, and 25; OEM class, dimension, and scale semantics remain unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_B5_RESERVED0_3 "0x191 byte 5 low three bits. Zero on every recorded active paired row; packed-field boundary guard. Sentinel value is seven.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_FIELD5_CODE5 "0x191 bits 43|5. Dynamic pair-local code with active values 9..30 and sentinel 31. It correlates with track age but fails the cross-route monotone lifecycle gate, so OEM meaning remains unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_B6_RESERVED0 "0x191 byte 6 low bit. Zero on every recorded active paired row; packed-field boundary guard. Sentinel value is zero.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_DESCRIPTOR1_CODE7 "0x191 bits 49|7. Second member of an identity-stable three-code descriptor tuple. Active values are 15 and 23; OEM class, dimension, and scale semantics remain unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 401 A191_PAIR_DESCRIPTOR2_CODE8 "0x191 bits 56|8. Third member of an identity-stable three-code descriptor tuple. Active values are 20, 45, and 120; OEM class, dimension, and scale semantics remain unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 402 A192_WORD0_RESERVED_ZERO3 "0x192 first 16-bit container top three bits. Zero on every active paired row on the recorded drives; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 402 A192_PAIR_RANGE_CODE13 "Big-endian 13-bit distance code, about 3/64 m (0.047 m) per code; smoothed and lagged (see message comment).";
CM_ SG_ 402 A192_WORD1_RESERVED_ZERO3 "0x192 second 16-bit container top three bits. Zero on every active paired row on the recorded drives; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 402 A192_PAIR_FIELD1_CODE13 "Bytes 2-3. Byte 2 (the high bits of this field) is a lateral bin of the target; byte 3 unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 403 A193_B0_RESERVED0 "0x193 byte 0 low bit. Zero on all recorded active and sentinel frames; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 403 A193_PAIR_SCORE_CODE7 "0x193 bits 1|7. Exact score-like code: active values are 91..100, same-identity transitions are almost always stable or unit steps, and sentinel value is 127. Route-stable survival stratification exists, but route-heldout evidence does not justify naming this OEM confidence or using it as validity, publication, or selection truth.";
CM_ SG_ 403 A193_B1_RESERVED0 "0x193 byte 1 low bit. Zero on all recorded active and sentinel frames; packed-field boundary guard.";
CM_ SG_ 403 A193_PAIR_TRACK_AGE7 "0x193 bits 9|7. Track-age-like counter: usually advances across nominal 60 ms cycles while identity is stable, plateaus at 126, and is 127 in the sentinel. Repeats and jumps occur; age may advance while the co-envelope 0x190 timestamp repeats. Native same-tag unsaturated examples advance through intervening sentinel output cycles; sentinel return need not reset age. Not elapsed time, a freshness gate, physical identity proof, or full OEM lifecycle/publication truth. Identity can migrate between output pairs.";
